cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository when using its analysis code or online supplements, and cite the original MeLiDos study when reusing the prepared data."
type: software
title: "MeLiDos chronotype analysis: online supplements and reproducible code"
authors:
  - family-names: Zauner
    given-names: Johannes
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2171-4566"
  - family-names: Spitschan
    given-names: Manuel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8572-9268"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tscnlab/ZaunerSpitschan_JBiolRhythms_2026"
url: "https://tscnlab.github.io/ZaunerSpitschan_JBiolRhythms_2026/"
date-released: 2026-11-11
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R analyses and a Quarto manuscript examining daily melanopic
  light exposure across chronotypes in the MeLiDos cohort. The project compares
  clock-time and corrected-midsleep alignment, work and free days, photoperiod
  moderation, conceptual phase-response-curve weighting, and sleep-diary
  sensitivity analyses. The manuscript is a working draft.
keywords:
  - chronotype
  - melanopic light exposure
  - photoperiod
  - circadian entrainment
  - sleep diary
  - Quarto
